@*
    =================================================================================================
     _Imports.razor  —  "using" directives shared by EVERY .razor file in this folder and below
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     What it is:
       Razor's own way of sharing @using (and other) directives: the compiler copies every line of
       this special file into each component in this folder and its sub-folders.  Each @using line below is silently added to every component under Components/, which is why
       the pages can write  CartService  or  Fmt.Money(...)  without their own @using lines.

     What the student sees on screen: nothing; this file renders no markup.
     Data source: none.

     Read next: App.razor (the root HTML document) and Routes.razor (the router).
    =================================================================================================
*@
@* Framework namespaces that the Blazor project template adds by default. *@
@using System.Net.Http
@using System.Net.Http.Json
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.Virtualization
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@* "using static" lets markup write  @rendermode="InteractiveServer"  instead of  RenderMode.InteractiveServer. *@
@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode
@* MiniShop namespaces: message contracts, our own components, and the Web services the pages inject. *@
@using MiniShop.Contracts
@using MiniShop.Web.Components
@using MiniShop.Web.Components.Layout
@using MiniShop.Web.Components.Developer
@using MiniShop.Web.Cart
@using MiniShop.Web.Queries
@using MiniShop.Web.ReadModel
@using MiniShop.Web.Projections
@using MiniShop.Web.Scenarios
@using MiniShop.Web.Services
